desc: Sub Plot Sub-Bass Synthesizer (mda SubSynth port) by chmaha
tags: bass sub octave divider synthesizer enhancer
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Adds synthesized sub-bass under the input. The summed input goes through a low-pass filter (Tune), and whenever the
  filtered bass is above Thresh it drives one of four generators, whose output is low-pass filtered again and added at
  Level to the dry signal (Dry Mix).
  Distort: a squared-up, distorted copy of the bass. Divide: a square-wave octave divider, one octave below.
  Invert: an octave divider that flips the filtered bass on every other cycle, softer than Divide.
  Key Osc: a sine oscillator at the Tune frequency, retriggered while the bass is above Thresh and fading out at the
  Release rate when it drops below.
  Ported from mda SubSynth by Paul Kellett (Maxim Digital Audio), via mda-effects
  https://github.com/pluginguru/mda-effects (MIT or GPLv2+)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
